From: Alexander Vickberg <wickbergster@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: do not force flow control on CPU ports

Flow control on CPU ports was unconditionally enabled regardless of
what was negotiated by phylink or what was specified in the fixed-link
node. Remove the dsa_is_cpu_port() override and let rx_pause and
tx_pause from phylink_mac_link_up() exclusively control the flow
control bits, consistent with how non-CPU ports are handled.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Vickberg <wickbergster@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1474,10 +1474,10 @@ qca8k_phylink_mac_link_up(struct phylink_config *config,
 		if (duplex == DUPLEX_FULL)
 			reg |= QCA8K_PORT_STATUS_DUPLEX;
 
-		if (rx_pause || dsa_port_is_cpu(dp))
+		if (rx_pause)
 			reg |= QCA8K_PORT_STATUS_RXFLOW;
 
-		if (tx_pause || dsa_port_is_cpu(dp))
+		if (tx_pause)
 			reg |= QCA8K_PORT_STATUS_TXFLOW;
 	}
 
